[THOUGHT] The Medical Analyst has now provided definitive objective evidence:  
- Polysomnography confirms *normal sleep efficiency* (ruling out primary insomnia, sleep apnea, or periodic limb movement disorder),  
- Melatonin levels are *elevated in the early evening*, which is the biological hallmark of Advanced Sleep-Wake Phase Disorder (ASWPD), and  
- Actigraphy corroborates advanced rest-activity timing.  
All eight evidence domains are now sufficiently covered:  
1) Chief complaint & onset → early sleepiness, lifelong pattern implied;  
2) Course → stable early sleep onset (~6 p.m.) and early wake time (confirmed by actigraphy + melatonin);  
3) Associated symptoms → none reported beyond timing;  
4) Past history → no neurological/psychiatric conditions;  
5) Medications → none relevant;  
6) Social/exposure → though not quantified, melatonin phase shift confirms endogenous circadian advance;  
7) Physical exam → not documented, but polysomnography and melatonin data make secondary causes highly unlikely;  
8) Labs/imaging → melatonin DLMO-equivalent finding + PSG + actigraphy provide conclusive circadian diagnosis.  
No critical gaps remain. I am now prepared to issue [FINISH].

[FINISH]

